<title>USA: Ball Corp Q4 loss widens, sales rise.</title>
<headline>Ball Corp Q4 loss widens, sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>MUNCIE, Ind. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary loss	$ 0.46     loss     $  0.01</p>
<p> Shr diluted loss	  0.42     loss	  0.01</p>
<p> Net loss		  13,900     loss	   300</p>
<p> Sales		    500,100		  470,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	30,494		   30,067</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	32,484		   30,067</p>
<p>	 (All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>	 12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr pri profit	  $ 0.70     loss	$ 0.72</p>
<p> Shr dil profit	    0.68     loss	  0.64</p>
<p> Net profit		21,300     loss	21,700</p>
<p> Sales		  2,184,400		2,045,800</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	30,314		   30,024</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted	32,357		   32,328</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: All net profit and net loss results include preferred dividend payments.</p>
<p>1996 Q4 loss includes loss from continuing operations equal to $0.89 a share and gain from discontinued operations equal to $0.43 a share.</p>
<p>1995 Q4 loss includes gain from continuing operations equal to $0.06 a share and loss from discontinued operations equal to $0.07 a share.</p>
<p>1996 year profit includes gain from continuing operations equal to $0.34 a share and gain from discontinued operations equal to $0.36 a share.</p>
<p>1995 year loss includes gain from continuing operations equal to $1.63 a share and a loss from discontinued operations equal to $2.35 a share.</p>
<p>		 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
